<style>body{font:13px -apple-system,sans-serif;margin:16px;color:#222}h2{margin:0 0 4px}h3{margin:14px 0 4px;color:#d9507a}
li{margin:3px 0}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#eee;background:#1e1e1e}}</style></head>
<body><h2>Pocket Pals 1.0.3</h2><p>Pets stay on their desktop</p><h3>Fixed</h3><ul><li>Pets really do stay on their desktop now. They could turn up on another Space or over a fullscreen app after your Mac woke from sleep, a display changed, or you hid and showed them. Pocket Pals now waits until you&#x27;re back on the pets&#x27; desktop before redrawing anything, and hiding pets fades them out in place instead of moving their window.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
